author={Alokush, Basem and Mughaid, Ala and AlZu’bi, Shadi},
booktitle={2025 3rd International Conference on Foundation and Large Language Models (FLLM)}, 
title={Fine-Tuned LLMs in Programming Education to Improve Student Performance in Syntax Mastery and Problem-Solving Skills}, 
year={2025},
volume={},
number={},
pages={845-850},
abstract={AI and particular LLMs is increasingly restructuring educational process. While GenAI has proved its ability to provide real-time code suggestions and explanations, using GenAI in programming education raises both opportunities and challenges. Students may use LLMs to bypass acquiring important skills, depend on AI generated code instead of developing themselves. This study investigates the impact of fine-tuned LLMs in programming education focusing on two important learning criteria (syntax mastery and problem-solving skills). The work investigates on how LLMs employed with domain-specific educational datasets to provide personalized, context-aware feed-back supporting students, while encouraging responsible and creative GenAI usage. The proposed approach is established within a student-centered educational framework where AI acts as a teaching assistant, reducing thinking load by explaining errors in natural language, while shifting teaching objectives towards creativity, debugging, and adaptation. For performance evaluation, experiments across three student levels (high school programming courses, undergraduate introductory courses, and advanced computer science classes) with three sections of 20 students each is conducted. The proposed work has been tested traditional instruction using real programming datasets and AI-augmented learning group using simulated coding tasks. The system performance is evaluated using several metrics such as creativity and engagement, problem-solving accuracy, syntax error reduction, and time to solve. The achieved results prove that fine-tuned LLMs improve student creativity and engagement significantly, where improvements in syntax mastery and logical problem-solving maintain the quality. The achievement suggested to integrate fine-tuned LLMs with responsible AI to improve programming education, and overcome traditional methods where more creative and reflective learners achieved.},
keywords={Performance evaluation;Codes;System performance;Education;Natural languages;Syntactics;Real-time systems;Problem-solving;Programming profession;Creativity;Fine-Tuned LLMs;Programming Education;Syntax Mastery;GenAI for Problem Solving;AI-Augmented Learning},
