abstract={Recently, programming methodologies are being increasingly introduced into children's education. For example, Scratch11https://scratch-mit-edu.ezproxy.lancs.ac.uk/ and The Hour of Code22https://hourofcode.com platforms have been adopted in many schools worldwide. However, the daunting problem remains: prolonged use of mobile phones increases the risk of smartphone addiction. This rising incorporation of program-ming alongside the aforementioned negative aspect of traditional serious games have demanded a healthier and more effective platform for programming education to enhance the learning experience of children. As a result, this paper introduces a serious game that incorporates Augmented Reality environments and optical character recognition technology (OCR) to limit screen time and visualize the written code in an efficient and more immersive manner. An experiment was conducted measuring the proposed system's effect on student's learning gain, player's experience, and usability relative to desktop environments. The results show a correlation between the use of the Kode- Arsystem and an increase in learning gain and a positive player experience. The results of system usability were inconclusive.},
