abstract={VIREX (Virtual Execution Console) is an integrated, terminal-based learning environment that illustrates the complete program execution life cycle—from high-level source code to low-level machine instructions—within a single interactive interface. It combines three core components: a compiler for the Orin programming language, the SASM assembler, and a custom virtual machine that emulates CPU registers, memory, stack operations, and system calls. This unified environment enables learners to observe and understand the interactions between compilation, assembly, and execution in real time. Central to this system is SASM (Simulated Assembly), which features a minimalist, rule-based instruction set and a streamlined assembly pipeline designed for educational clarity and precision. It supports compile-time functions such as len(str), ref(reg), and value(reg) for operand evaluation/operand intent classification, and generates a visualizable abstract syntax tree (AST) for every file, making the internal structure of assembly programs transparent and educationally valuable.},
