abstract={With the rapid development of artificial intelligence technology in the field of education, AI has shown great potential in programming education. However, the traditional pair programming method cannot provide immediate feedback and has certain limitations. This study proposes an innovative AI-assisted learning method, aiming to enhance students' programming learning experience and efficiency through the assistance of AI. This study employed a hierarchical guided AI tool based on large language models and adopted a quasi-experimental design to investigate the impact of AI methods on students' academic performance, self-efficacy, and learning interest. A study was conducted on 80 undergraduate students of the C language programming course. Two classes were randomly assigned to AI assisted pair programming (n=38) and human-human pair programming (n=42). The research results show that artificial intelligence assistance can effectively improve students' programming performance, self-efficacy and programming interest. This research provides strong practical guidance for integrating AI-assisted learning into programming courses in colleges and universities.},
