abstract={While adaptive AI tutoring can enhance learning outcomes in fundamental computer science, excessive reliance on AI-generated solutions may reduce cognitive engagement, which is essential for deep understanding. To address this, we introduce the Encouraging and Engaging Assignment Assistant (E2A2), an AI-powered tutoring system designed to foster active learning, structured guidance, and academic integrity in introductory programming courses. Unlike conventional AI systems that provide complete solutions, E2A2 employs step-by-step guidance, retrieval-augmented generation, and adaptive feedback to promote meaningful engagement with learning modules rather than passive answer consumption. By integrating course materials, assignment guidelines, and student progress tracking, E2A2 delivers context-aware, personalized support that strengthens problem-solving and programming skills. By redefining AI’s role from an answer provider to a learning facilitator, E2A2 offers a scalable, ethical approach to AI-driven tutoring, bridging the gap between AI assistance and authentic student learning.},
keywords={Ethics;Adaptive systems;Navigation;Active learning;Retrieval augmented generation;Programming;Problem-solving;Artificial intelligence;Guidelines;AI Tutoring;Active Learning;Structured Guidance;AI Ethics},
