abstract={This research proposes and validates a design framework for an adaptive intelligence application courseware aim to enhance learning productivity in computer programming (JAVA) of students taking diploma courses. A mixed-methods approach was used to address critical gaps including on challenges encountered in technical concepts and the limitations of static Learning Management Systems (LMS) in resource-constrained environments. With participatory surveys, the initial analysis, algorithmic thinking are major concerns of the students in programming concepts. On clustering analysis results distinct students struggle on foundational concepts which are very important in first phase on learning programming like java. The developed proposed courseware framework, utilizing Java programming language is align on industry relevance, leverages an adaptive learning application to dynamically tailor on courseware content, efficient pacing, and feedback mechanism based on the student's real-time struggle profile. This research structured approach provides a scalable and validated solution for computer programming education toward personalized, competency-based IT industry standard in the Philippines.},
