abstract={Competitive programming is a popular method of honing coding and problem-solving skills that can help a programmer in their future work in software development, especially in competitions or interviews. Even though students are actively participating in their education, they are frequently left to “figure it out” because they are not receiving real-time support, responses might not be received promptly, and there are few options for developing customized next steps. All of this makes it more difficult to develop these abilities. In this paper, we describe a Real-Time AI Coaching System that takes a significant leap toward addressing the issues in feedback and assessment by providing immediate intelligent feedback to programmers while they write and debug code. Testing the system showed improvements in user engagement, accuracy, and efficiency during problem-solving. Additionally, this paper examines existing platforms, compares them with our proposed solution, and highlights its potential to transform competitive programming training. This Model will serve a dual role; tutor and helping to advance a student's programming competency. It will be valuable for the advancement of educational technology in computer science.},
