pages={1192-1198},
abstract={Computer programming can be a difficult and intimidating subject for students. Online resources are ideal for theoretical knowledge but need a virtual programming environment to put things into practice. This paper presents the usability evaluation of Virtual Lab (VL) as an integrated component of learning management system (LMS) for teaching programming to students at undergraduate, and postgraduate levels. We used the System Usability Scale (SUS), a validated measurement of usability. Four hundred users were classified as either familiar or unfamiliar with the platform. The usability score for experienced users was 79.2 and for newcomers -- 78.1, so familiar users had a very small advantage over newcomers. The general alphabetical score of B signifies decent usability, verifying the fact that the device is a successful instructional assist. The results warrant the expansion of Virtual Labs in programming education for improved learning outcomes.},
