abstract={With the popularization of programming education, the issue of code plagiarism detection and similarity analysis in student assignments has become increasingly prominent. Traditional code plagiarism detection methods face limitations when dealing with complex code structures and semantics, while the rapid development of deep learning techniques offers new solutions for this field. This paper reviews recent deep learning-based approaches for code similarity detection, with a focus on analyzing the advantages and limitations of different models, including Siamese neural networks, graph neural networks, and their applications in cross-language clone detection. Research indicates that deep learning methods demonstrate significant advantages in improving detection accuracy and efficiency, but challenges such as interpretability and generalization capability remain to be addressed. Future research directions will concentrate on optimizing feature extraction methods, enhancing model interpretability, and developing cross-language detection technologies.},
